  "transcript": [
    {
      "turn": 0,
      "role": "patient",
      "text": "Hello. I've had this cough for ages and I'm starting to worry about it."
    },
    {
      "turn": 1,
      "role": "interviewer",
      "text": "How long have you had this cough?"
    },
    {
      "turn": 1,
      "role": "patient",
      "text": "Five weeks. It started after a heavy cold, and it's still not gone."
    },
    {
      "turn": 2,
      "role": "interviewer",
      "text": "Have you had any other symptoms along with the cough, like fever, chest pain, or shortness of breath?"
    },
    {
      "turn": 2,
      "role": "patient",
      "text": "I've been a bit short of breath climbing two flights of stairs. No fever and no chest pain."
    },
    {
      "turn": 3,
      "role": "interviewer",
      "text": "Have you noticed any changes in the color or amount of mucus you're coughing up?"
    },
    {
      "turn": 3,
      "role": "patient",
      "text": "I've coughed up some phlegm with a few streaks of blood twice this week."
    },
    {
      "turn": 4,
      "role": "interviewer",
      "text": "Have you been exposed to anyone with a cough or cold recently, or have you been in any environments that might irritate your lungs, like smoke or dust?"
    },
    {
      "turn": 4,
      "role": "patient",
      "text": "I think the cough might be worse because of the dust in the van. I've been driving a lot lately."
    },
    {
      "turn": 5,
      "role": "interviewer",
      "text": "Have you experienced any recent weight loss, night sweats, or fatigue along with your cough?"
    },
    {
      "turn": 5,
      "role": "patient",
      "text": "No, I haven't lost weight, and I don't get night sweats. I feel tired sometimes, but not really fatigued."
    },
    {
      "turn": 6,
      "role": "interviewer",
      "text": "Have you had any recent changes in your lifestyle, such as stress, lack of sleep, or changes in diet?"
    },
    {
      "turn": 6,
      "role": "patient",
      "text": "I've been working long hours driving, so I haven't been getting enough sleep. I'm not sure if that's making the cough worse."
    },
    {
      "turn": 7,
      "role": "interviewer",
      "text": "Have you smoked cigarettes or been exposed to secondhand smoke recently?"
    },
    {
      "turn": 7,
      "role": "patient",
      "text": "I stopped smoking ten years ago, but I used to smoke ten a day. I don't smoke now, but I'm not sure if secondhand smoke from the van is affecting me."
    },
    {
      "turn": 8,
      "role": "interviewer",
      "text": "Have you had any recent medical tests, such as a chest X-ray or blood work, related to your cough?"
    },
    {
      "turn": 8,
      "role": "patient",
      "text": "No, I haven't had any tests yet. I just want to know what's going on with my cough."
    },
    {
      "turn": 9,
      "role": "interviewer",
      "text": "Thank you for sharing all that information. You've described a cough that has lasted five weeks, started after a cold, and has been accompanied by shortness of breath, occasional blood-tinged phlegm, and exposure to dust in a van. You also mentioned working long hours with limited sleep and a history of smoking.  \n\n[HISTORY COMPLETE]"
    }
  ],
